# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
JM105 Figure 2 v4.1 — cross-font no-overlap repair renderer.

Figure 2 panel identities are locked to the current PowerPoint:
A = JM104 replicative-lifespan curves.
B = age-effect versus old-cell CR-suppression scatter.
C = four-quadrant interpretation schematic.
D = ranked named candidates.
E = restored accepted PowerPoint raw-profile panel asset.
F = selection-gate hierarchy in the accepted checklist visual language.

RNA scope fence:
Only total / rRNA-depleted JM105 sources are used for B/D/F.
Poly-A, P-versus-T, mRNA-like, and P−T constructs are out of scope.

Definitions:
NMD_hidden = IR(upf1Δ) − IR(UPF1+)
candidate_score = min(aging_effect, CR_suppression)
Panel F contrast = computed (+MUD1 CR-suppression) vs (mud1Δ CR-suppression);
Figure 2F remains the locked gate-hierarchy panel and does not display this contrast.

Render contract:
- fixed canvas sizes declared below;
- automatic tight cropping is not used;
- SVG text remains editable;
- transparent SVG/PDF/PNG plus white preview;
- hard collision gate runs before any panel is accepted.
"""

